{"id": 117742, "acmi_id": "B2003346", "title": "[Gadsden Family Home Movie Collection: Reel 37]", "title_annotation": "", "slug": "gadsden-family-home-movie-collection-reel-37", "creator_credit": "Ronald Gadsden and Stanley Gadsden", "credit_line": "", "headline_credit": "Australia, c. 1972", "record_type": "work", "type": "Film", "is_on_display": false, "last_on_display_place": null, "last_on_display_date": null, "is_context_indigenous": false, "material_description": "", "unpublished": false, "external": false, "first_production_date": null, "brief_description": "<p>The Gadsden Company has a long and proud history of manufacture, dating back to its foundation by Jabez Gadsden in 1879. The company pioneered tinplate printing in Australia, and produced the first printed can the country had seen. By 1936 the company had twelve factories spread throughout Australia and New Zealand.</p>\n<p>The company’s success allowed two generations of Gadsden family men – Stanley Gadsden and his son Ronald – to pursue their interest in amateur filmmaking (a relatively expensive hobby for the time). The two cameramen captured the family’s children, homes, many of its major events and holidays on film.</p>\n<p>A collection of the films made by these Gadsden family photographers has been donated to ACMI by Chris Gadsden (Ronald’s son). The films comprise a fascinating assortment of imagery that provides a window into bygone days and customs.</p>\n<p>This film shows sailing activities at the Davey&#8217;s Bay Yacht Club as well as yacht racing off the Mornington Peninsula, Victoria.</p>\n<p>This film was originally made using Super 8mm film.</p>\n<p>Selected highlights list:<br />\n00:01:05:00 yacht sailing into bay with cliff top houses in background<br />\n00:04:10:00 hoisting a yacht into the water</p>", "constellations_primary": [], "constellations_other": [], "recommendations": [], "title_for_label": "<p>[Gadsden Family Home Movie Collection: Reel 37]</p>", "creator_credit_for_label": "<p>Ronald Gadsden and Stanley Gadsden</p>", "headline_credit_for_label": "<p>Australia, c. 1972</p>", "description": "<p>The Gadsden Company has a long and proud history of manufacture, dating back to its foundation by Jabez Gadsden in 1879. The company pioneered tinplate printing in Australia, and produced the first printed can the country had seen. By 1936 the company had twelve factories spread throughout Australia and New Zealand.</p>\n<p>The company’s success allowed two generations of Gadsden family men – Stanley Gadsden and his son Ronald – to pursue their interest in amateur filmmaking (a relatively expensive hobby for the time). The two cameramen captured the family’s children, homes, many of its major events and holidays on film.</p>\n<p>A collection of the films made by these Gadsden family photographers has been donated to ACMI by Chris Gadsden (Ronald’s son). The films comprise a fascinating assortment of imagery that provides a window into bygone days and customs.</p>\n<p>This film shows sailing activities at the Davey&#8217;s Bay Yacht Club as well as yacht racing off the Mornington Peninsula, Victoria.</p>\n<p>This film was originally made using Super 8mm film.</p>\n<p>Selected highlights list:<br />\n00:01:05:00 yacht sailing into bay with cliff top houses in background<br />\n00:04:10:00 hoisting a yacht into the water</p>", "description_for_label": ["<p>The Gadsden Company has a long and proud history of manufacture, dating back to its foundation by Jabez Gadsden in 1879. The company pioneered tinplate printing in Australia, and produced the first printed can the country had seen. By 1936 the company had twelve factories spread throughout Australia and New Zealand.</p>\n<p>The company’s success allowed two generations of Gadsden family men – Stanley Gadsden and his son Ronald – to pursue their interest in amateur filmmaking (a relatively expensive hobby for the time). The two cameramen captured the family’s children, homes, many of its major events and holidays on film.</p>\n<p>A collection of the films made by these Gadsden family photographers has been donated to ACMI by Chris Gadsden (Ronald’s son). The films comprise a fascinating assortment of imagery that provides a window into bygone days and customs.</p>\n<p>This film shows sailing activities at the Davey&#8217;s Bay Yacht Club as well as yacht racing off the Mornington Peninsula, Victoria.</p>\n<p>This film was originally made using Super 8mm film.</p>\n<p>Selected highlights list:<br />\n00:01:05:00 yacht sailing into bay with cliff top houses in background<br />\n00:04:10:00 hoisting a yacht into the water</p>"], "credit_line_for_label": "", "details": [{"label": "Duration", "display_values": ["00:23:20:00"]}, {"label": "Subject categories", "display_values": ["Amateur & Student Films&nbsp;→ Amateur films", "Communications, Infrastructure, & Transport&nbsp;→ Sailing", "History&nbsp;→ Australia - History - 1972-1975", "History&nbsp;→ Mornington Peninsula Region (Vic.) - History", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Sailing", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Sailing, Single-handed", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Sports", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Sports - Australia - History", "Hobbies, Recreation & Sport&nbsp;→ Yacht racing", "Places&nbsp;→ Port Phillip Bay (Vic.)", "Short films", "Short films&nbsp;→ Short films - Australia"]}, {"label": "Sound/audio", "display_values": ["Silent"]}, {"label": "Colour", "display_values": ["Colour"]}], "stats": {"tap_count": 0}, "links": [], "creators_primary": [{"id": 1862605, "name": "Ronald Gadsden", "creator_id": 84292, "creator_wikidata_id": null, "role": "creator", "role_id": 968, "is_primary": true}, {"id": 1862604, "name": "Stanley Gadsden", "creator_id": 84291, "creator_wikidata_id": null, "role": "creator", "role_id": 968, "is_primary": true}], "creators_other": [], "video_links": [{"id": 2874, "name": "ACMI External Digital Access Copy", "uri": "https://youtu.be/FukV1zIG54s"}], "me